    "experience_text": "Use the matched guidance together where supported by the current task and source. If advice conflicts, resolve it against the concrete requirements and explain the choice; do not combine incompatible obligations.\n\nMatched experience 722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R01 [Applicability]\nThe repair targets panel progress, while queue records, queued notices and public transfer behavior must remain unchanged.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R02 [Event relation]\nKeep records and notices bound to the entry file, attempt, visit and command kind. Display changes must not alter their fields or cardinality.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R03 [Preservation]\nHistorical transfer records are {fileId, attemptId, visitId, kind}. These fields belong to those cases' contracts, not a default API for new systems.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R04 [Exclusion]\nWithout separate authorization, do not add byteCount or infer new business records from file.size. Passing display checks does not establish queue preservation. Automatic Contracts, AST hints and evaluation observations are not new business requirements. Do not modify implementation during analysis or replace the current contract with hidden scores or reference patches.\n\n722b82960892efbb479e9b3a583e36eedd7a028da0ed9e96cc8f07a6e48308ca:R05 [Verification]\nCompare record shape, cardinality, queued notices and returned handles across selection, retry, cancellation and navigation reentry.\n\n\nMatched experience 36ca20e456a49b2f355ed2266ee2b7841d5f2c29748c257be566a3846f6e5af5\n36ca20e456a49b2f355ed2266ee2b7841d5f2c29748c257be566a3846f6e5af5:R01 [Applicability]\nA shared query can start a replacement attempt while deferred results or retry callbacks from an old attempt may still arrive.\n\n36ca20e456a49b2f355ed2266ee2b7841d5f2c29748c257be566a3846f6e5af5:R02 [Event relation]\nOn continuation and completion, check actual attempt identity and settlement state. Cancellation and completion belong to the originating attempt; an old callback must not become the replacement's data or settlement.\n\n36ca20e456a49b2f355ed2266ee2b7841d5f2c29748c257be566a3846f6e5af5:R03 [Preservation]\nPreserve cancellation restoration, legitimate current results and later observer reuse. Keep the repair within product source and existing public behavior.\n\n36ca20e456a49b2f355ed2266ee2b7841d5f2c29748c257be566a3846f6e5af5:R04 [Exclusion]\nEqual query keys do not isolate attempts. Do not suppress the current attempt or permitted background cache updates merely to block stale completion.\n\n36ca20e456a49b2f355ed2266ee2b7841d5f2c29748c257be566a3846f6e5af5:R05 [Verification]\nRelease an old completion after replacement or cancellation, and interleave old/new retries and reconnect. Check exactly-once originating-attempt settlement and data from the current attempt.\n\n\nMatched experience bbd6eee9031ebf434c55cd29d1c35f132f9a7b79c441a16f3903e7d6992b822a\nbbd6eee9031ebf434c55cd29d1c35f132f9a7b79c441a16f3903e7d6992b822a:R01 [Applicability]\nThe current interface specifies synchronous initial online entry, asynchronous completion and paused continuation, and different readiness conditions for initial and resumed execution.\n\nbbd6eee9031ebf434c55cd29d1c35f132f9a7b79c441a16f3903e7d6992b822a:R02 [Event relation]\nPreserve the initial network-mode check, network and focus gates for continuation, explicit retry handles, and Promise-turn or native-equivalent asynchronous timing.\n\nbbd6eee9031ebf434c55cd29d1c35f132f9a7b79c441a16f3903e7d6992b822a:R03 [Preservation]\nWhere these modes exist, always permits offline execution; offlineFirst permits initial offline entry but retries may pause. Preserve supported interfaces, dependencies and build/test configuration.\n\nbbd6eee9031ebf434c55cd29d1c35f132f9a7b79c441a16f3903e7d6992b822a:R04 [Exclusion]\nDo not repair departure cancellation by delaying every initial entry, resuming paused tasks synchronously or conflating retry and initial-entry gates. Do not invent these APIs for systems that lack the modes.\n\nbbd6eee9031ebf434c55cd29d1c35f132f9a7b79c441a16f3903e7d6992b822a:R05 [Verification]\nCheck synchronous online entry, asynchronous completion, connectivity without focus, focus restoration, always/offlineFirst, explicit retry cancellation and already-queued continuation separately.\n",
